IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sge-p10a-364`

-- Tests of s 364 (Part 10A, Transfer of registration: certificates). Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion,
-- before the run. The company is registered on 1 March 2027; 60 days after that is 30 April 2027 (31 days to 1 April, 29 more to 30 April).
-- A notice is served on 10 June 2027; 10 days after that is 20 June 2027.

§ `Section 364(1): the certificates`

-- Arguments: registered as a holder of existing shares; registered as a holder of existing debentures.
#ASSERT `s 364(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 364(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 364(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a registered holder at the date of registration: the text names its persons and says nothing of anyone else.
#ASSERT `s 364(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 364(1) the last day for completing and having ready for delivery the certificates` (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS Date 30 4 2027

-- Arguments: date of registration; the certificates are ready; the date they were ready; the date asked.
-- Ready on the last day: in time.
#ASSERT `s 364(1) the company has completed and has ready for delivery the certificates within 60 days after the date of registration` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 30 4 2027) (Date 1 8 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Ready well inside the period.
#ASSERT `s 364(1) the company has completed and has ready for delivery the certificates within 60 days after the date of registration` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 1 8 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Ready the day after the last day: too late.
#ASSERT `s 364(1) the company has completed and has ready for delivery the certificates within 60 days after the date of registration` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 1 5 2027) (Date 1 8 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not ready: on the last day the period still runs; the day after, the duty has been missed.
#ASSERT `s 364(1) the company has completed and has ready for delivery the certificates within 60 days after the date of registration` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 30 4 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 364(1) the company has completed and has ready for delivery the certificates within 60 days after the date of registration` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 5 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The duty as a rule: 60 days from the date of registration (AT 0). Ready on day 60: in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 364(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the certificates within 60 days after the date of registration` "Acme Pte. Ltd." AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 364(1) complete and have ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of all persons registered as holders of existing shares or debentures` AT 60

-- Not ready and the clock reaches day 61: breached.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 364(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the certificates within 60 days after the date of registration` "Acme Pte. Ltd." AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 61

-- Ready on day 61: too late, so breached.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 364(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the certificates within 60 days after the date of registration` "Acme Pte. Ltd." AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 364(1) complete and have ready for delivery appropriate certificates in respect of all persons registered as holders of existing shares or debentures` AT 61

§ `Section 364(2): the prior certificates cease to be operative`

-- Arguments: the prior certificate is in respect of shares or debentures whose new certificates have been delivered; the new certificates have been delivered.
#ASSERT `s 364(2) the prior certificate has ceased to be operative` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 364(2) the prior certificate has ceased to have any validity for the purposes of this Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not yet delivered: the "Upon" is not met, so the prior certificate has not ceased.
#ASSERT `s 364(2) the prior certificate has ceased to be operative` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 364(2) the prior certificate has ceased to have any validity for the purposes of this Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A certificate in respect of other shares or debentures: outside the subsection.
#ASSERT `s 364(2) the prior certificate has ceased to be operative` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 364(2) the prior certificate has ceased to have any validity for the purposes of this Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 364(3): bearer share warrants are void`

-- Arguments: the document is a bearer share warrant of the kind described; it was issued by the foreign corporate entity; the date issued; the date of registration.
#ASSERT `s 364(3) the share warrant is void` TRUE TRUE (Date 28 2 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Issued on the date of registration itself: not "before" it.
#ASSERT `s 364(3) the share warrant is void` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Issued after registration: not caught.
#ASSERT `s 364(3) the share warrant is void` TRUE TRUE (Date 2 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not issued by the foreign corporate entity: not caught.
#ASSERT `s 364(3) the share warrant is void` TRUE FALSE (Date 28 2 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a bearer warrant of the kind described.
#ASSERT `s 364(3) the share warrant is void` FALSE TRUE (Date 28 2 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 364(4): the Court's order to make good the default`

-- Arguments: a notice has been served; the date served; the company has made good the default; the date it did; the date asked.
-- Made good on the last day of the 10: no failure.
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) TRUE (Date 20 6 2027) (Date 1 9 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Made good the day after the last day: a failure.
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) TRUE (Date 21 6 2027) (Date 1 9 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not made good: on the last day the 10 days still run; the day after, the company has failed.
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 20 6 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 21 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No notice served: no such failure.
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the company has failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice` FALSE (Date 10 6 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 21 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Arguments: the company has failed (as the subsection reads); the application is by the person entitled.
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the Court may make an order directing the company and any officer of the company to make good the default` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No failure: the "If" is not met.
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the Court may make an order directing the company and any officer of the company to make good the default` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A failure, but nobody entitled has applied.
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the Court may make an order directing the company and any officer of the company to make good the default` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Whom the order may direct.
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the order may direct the person to make good the default` `s 364(4) the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the order may direct the person to make good the default` `s 364(4) an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the order may direct the person to make good the default` `s 364(4) an officer of the company who is not in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the order may direct the person to make good the default` `s 364(4) another person` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Who may bear the costs.
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the order may provide that the costs of and incidental to the application are to be borne by the person` `s 364(4) the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the order may provide that the costs of and incidental to the application are to be borne by the person` `s 364(4) an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the order may provide that the costs of and incidental to the application are to be borne by the person` `s 364(4) an officer of the company who is not in default` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 364(4) the order may provide that the costs of and incidental to the application are to be borne by the person` `s 364(4) another person` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The order as a rule: a time of 14 days is specified (AT 0). Made good on day 14: in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 364(4) the company must make good the default within the time the order specifies` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 364(4) make good the default in complying with section 364` AT 14

-- Not made good and the clock reaches day 15: breached.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 364(4) the company must make good the default within the time the order specifies` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 14 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15

-- An officer directed by the same order: made good on day 14, in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 364(4) the officer must make good the default within the time the order specifies` "Lim Wei" 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Officer "Lim Wei" DOES `s 364(4) make good the default in complying with section 364` AT 14

-- The officer does nothing and the clock reaches day 15: breached.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 364(4) the officer must make good the default within the time the order specifies` "Lim Wei" 14 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15
